WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:11.608
Routers, which route traffic between networks, have a wide variety of speeds in which they can transmit data. Some routers can transmit data in excess of 1 Gbps.

00:11.608 --> 00:20.447
But, here is the thing to consider with router speeds: they, like other devices, can only transmit data as fast as the media connected to them.

00:20.447 --> 00:30.887
For example, say you have an 802.11n router, which can reach speeds of up to 600 Mbps wirelessly. And, that router has some Ethernet ports.

00:30.887 --> 00:42.101
Let's assume, for the sake of argument, that those are Fast Ethernet ports. Well, in that case, the wireless connection will be faster, as Fast Ethernet is 100 Mbps speed.

00:42.101 --> 00:46.750
Quite a difference. For router speeds, just understand that most routers, speed-wise,

00:46.750 --> 00:52.259
are going to be at the mercy of the media plugged into them or the wireless devices connected to them.

00:52.259 --> 00:58.413
In other words, you may often not get the top speeds as advertised by the device itself.

